        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "Walking down from the overpass to the St. George-bound platform and Arthur Kill Road entrance at the west end of the Arthur Kill station on the Main Branch of the Staten Island Railway (SIR / SIRT), along Arthur Kill Road / Ellis Street between Lion Street and Barnard Avenue (at approximately Nashville Street) in Tottenville, Staten Island. This large structure distinguishes this station from the older SIR stations, resembling <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FullertonTrainBridge.jpg\" title=\"File:FullertonTrainBridge.jpg\">other suburban intermodal stations</a>. Although this structure is large and tall, it consists simply of a metal truss frame and glass panels, missing the \"meat\" of for example the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MTA_Completes_Re-NEW-vation_at_Howard_Beach_A_Station.jpg\" title=\"File:MTA Completes Re-NEW-vation at Howard Beach A Station.jpg\">Howard Beach – JFK Airport station overpass</a>.",
